  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery includes a 'sure outcome'—that is, an outcome that occurs with 100% probability. In Lottery A, no outcome occurs with 100% probability: -4000€ (25%), -2000€ (25%), and 0€ (50%). In Lottery B, there is also no sure outcome: -6000€ (25%) and 0€ (75%). Therefore, neither lottery contains a sure outcome. Since the condition of having a sure outcome is not met in either lottery, the decision reason cannot be applied—the reason only comes into play if at least one lottery has a sure outcome. Thus, the reason would either be indifferent (if both had sure outcomes) or prefer the one with the sure outcome. But here, no such basis exists for preference according to this reason.",
